1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,900
On Spain's high northern plateau, in Castilla y León,

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:07,700
more than six hundred wind and solar installations share the same sky.

3
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:10,600
Their hardest days are the calm, grey ones,

4
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,900
when there is little wind and little sun at the same time.

5
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,400
Are those days becoming more common?

6
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:20,400
AETHRA puts the question to twenty-five years of NASA data.

7
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,400
The answer: no detectable change. Insufficient evidence.

8
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,700
Not proof that nothing is changing.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:29,000
Just what the data can defend.
